244628.missionDescription:
CNH is a world-class equipment and services company that sustainably advances the noble work of agriculture and construction workers. The Company provides the strategic direction, R&D capabilities, and investments that enable the success of its core Brands. Around the world, CNH Industrial brands are the driving force behind construction and agriculture. The innovation and efficiency they bring to the noble work of farming and building helps other areas of the global economy to reach their full potential. The Sales Administration Specialist (SSA) is a resource operating within the Commercial Operations dep.. 
She/He represents the main connection between Dealers, Distributors, Commercial team as well as with other internal deps. (eg. demand planning, pricing, logistics, Capital/Trade Finance), having in charge the whole order management process from entry/collection up to invoicing and distribution. 
She/He is expected to gain full awareness of market trends, sales volumes and distribution peculiarity, addressing opportunities and risks in order to proactively contribute to the achievement of the sales target of the Region. 
The main responsibilities of SSA role are:
	Order collection - SSA supports the Dealers in their order entry activity and validates the orders received, assessing possible match with company stock rather then addressing their production request to the plant, so as to optimize expected lead time and company stock management
	Order portfolio management – SSA manages order portfolio up to invoicing, promoting opportunities, assessing credit/manufacturing/logistics risks and proactively advising possible alternatives to offset/mitigate them, participating actively to the sales target achievement;
	Invoicing Management – SSA follows up invoicing process, assessing Dealer solvibility/credit release and deploying terms and conditions (prices, discounts, incoterms) in line with commercial policy and revenue recognition; 
	Transport supervision – SSA transmits instructions to set up and organize units transportation (outbound call-off) and supports document collection/preparation for customs clearance. She/He also follows up urgent transport needs, coordinating requests from Dealers and internal departments (eg. logistics, marketing) for units to be shipped to customers, trade fairs, open days, demos within mandatory deadlines; 
	Training activities & events - SSA provides training activities referred to the main sales platforms/tools. She/He also takes part to B2B initiatives (events, fairs, meetings, etc.) upon request.

