247391.missionDescription:
To support the development of our activities in Italy, we are looking for a Construction Engineer / Project Manager to join a major high-tech industrial construction programme in the Milan area, sicily or Malta.
You will work on a technically demanding project involving advanced industrial facilities, with challenges linked to microelectronics, data centres and artificial intelligence infrastructure.
This position offers the opportunity to take on a key role within the construction management team and contribute directly to the successful delivery of a complex international project.

Responsibilities :
Working closely with the client, contractors and the wider project team, you will:
•	Proactively address construction-site issues in coordination with the client, contractors and engineering teams;
•	Identify potential technical, organizational and contractual challenges at an early stage;
•	Analyze and mitigate technical, schedule and interface-related risks;
•	Implement and monitor project processes to ensure quality, compliance and timely delivery;
•	Coordinate interfaces between the different project stakeholders, including planning, process engineering, design coordination and construction teams;
•	Contribute to the financial and administrative management of the project, including subcontractor approvals, quotation reviews, payment assessments and cost monitoring;
•	Prepare and review documentation relating to design changes, variations and additional works;
•	Monitor progress and escalate critical issues to the relevant decision-makers;
•	Support coordination meetings and provide clear reporting on project status, risks and priorities;
•	Depending on your experience, coordinate part of the site or project management team.

247391.missionProfile:
•	You hold a Master’s degree in civil engineering, building engineering, construction engineering or a related field;
•	You have at least one experience in construction, project management or works supervision, preferably on industrial, high-tech or technically complex building projects;
•	You have a strong understanding of construction processes, multidisciplinary interfaces, scheduling, quality management and project risk;
•	You are able to work autonomously in a demanding, fast-moving project environment;
•	You combine practical problem-solving skills with genuine technical curiosity;
•	You are proactive, adaptable and comfortable managing several stakeholders and priorities simultaneously;
•	You have strong interpersonal, listening and communication skills;
•	You are fluent in English and able to operate effectively in an international project environment;
•	Knowledge of Italian and previous experience in Italy would be an advantage

246970.missionDescription:
